  "invariant": "For x<r: x+c and x≥r: ax²+bx+q, bijection R→R requires ar²+br+q=r+c, a>0 and -b/(2a)≤r.",
  "proof": [
    "The first branch maps (-∞,r) bijectively onto (-∞,r+c).",
    "The second branch must map [r,∞) bijectively onto [r+c,∞), forcing the boundary value to match.",
    "The right quadratic has range [r+c,∞) and is injective on [r,∞) exactly when a>0 and its vertex is at or to the left of r.",
    "Substituting the boundary equation into the vertex inequality yields a≥(q-r-c)/r² for each candidate; minimum occurs at vertex r."
